  "statement": "The Harness's trajectory is a view of a durable log, and the pane now says so: a strip above the trajectory states how many events it holds, the seq range, where the cursor is and whether it is following the stream, showing a re-read, or showing a snapshot the log would not resume from; the strip opens into one row per held event, oldest first, and a row points at its own card; every retained event draws - including the twenty-five types this pane used to drop on the floor, which now reach a recorded-event card instead of a blank space; Replay re-reads the log from its first retained event and rebuilds the view from it without duplicating one; and a frame that lands while the reader is scrolled up no longer moves them, with one control, Jump to latest, as the only thing that does.",
